            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Hmm, that wasn't meant to be the case. I've fixed it here:\n\n\n[edac: Expose pldm_edac_crc32_validate() symbol in the shared library ABI](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/91779)\n\nCan you review that so we can get it merged, then you can rebase this change and adjust the commit message?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "reviewed and rebased, message adjusted \u2714\n\nThings look to be working as expected\n\n\n```\n[alexander@alexanderarchlinux libpldm]$ ldd build-fuzz/tests/fuzz/fuzz_cpp\n\tlinux-vdso.so.1 (0x00007fda4dc3f000)\n\tlibstdc++.so.6 => /usr/lib/libstdc++.so.6 (0x00007fda4ca00000)\n\tlibpldm++.so.0 => /home/alexander/upstreaming/libpldm/build-fuzz/tests/fuzz/../../bindings/cpp/libpldm++.so.0 (0x00007fda4dbda000)\n\tlibm.so.6 => /usr/lib/libm.so.6 (0x00007fda4c8cd000)\n\tlibresolv.so.2 => /usr/lib/libresolv.so.2 (0x00007fda4dbc6000)\n\tlibgcc_s.so.1 => /usr/lib/libgcc_s.so.1 (0x00007fda4db99000)\n\tlibc.so.6 => /usr/lib/libc.so.6 (0x00007fda4c600000)\n\t/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 => /usr/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 (0x00007fda4dc41000)\n\tlibpldm.so.0 => /home/alexander/upstreaming/libpldm/build-fuzz/tests/fuzz/../../bindings/cpp/../../src/libpldm.so.0 (0x00007fda4c200000)\n```\n```\n[alexander@alexanderarchlinux libpldm]$ nm --line-numbers build-fuzz/tests/fuzz/fuzz_cpp | grep crc32\n00000000002dbd88 T pldm_edac_crc32_validate\t/home/alexander/upstreaming/libpldm/build-fuzz/../tests/fuzz/fuzz_cpp.cpp:10\n```\n\nSomewhat related, i also tried to find coverage information\n\n```\nLLVM_PROFILE_FILE=default.profraw ./build-fuzz/tests/fuzz/fuzz_cpp -max_total_time=5 -max_len=150 ~/upstreaming/libpldm-fuzz/\n\nllvm-profdata merge -sparse default.profraw -o default.profdata\n\nllvm-cov show ./build-fuzz/tests/fuzz/fuzz_cpp -instr-profile=default.profdata      -format=text > fuzz-coverage.txt\n```\n\nand there it says it did not hit my override\n\n```\n   10|       |extern \"C\" int pldm_edac_crc32_validate(uint32_t expected\n   11|       |                                        __attribute__((unused)),\n   12|       |                                        const void* data\n   13|       |                                        __attribute__((unused)),\n   14|       |                                        size_t size __attribute__((unused)))\n   15|      0|{\n   16|      0|    return 0;\n   17|      0|} \n   18|       |  \n```\n\nmeanwhile the consumePackage was run quite often\n```\n  130|   952k|    std::expected<std::unique_ptr<pldm::fw_update::Package>,\n  131|   952k|                  pldm::fw_update::PackageParserError>\n  132|   952k|        res = pldm::fw_update::PackageParser::parse(\n  133|   952k|            p, pldm::fw_update::PackagePin::v1);\n  134|       |\n  135|   952k|    if (!res.has_value())\n  136|   949k|    {   \n  137|   949k|        free(package);\n  138|   949k|        return 0;\n  139|   949k|    }       \n  140|       |\n  141|  2.78k|    consumePackage(res.value());\n```\n\nso i assume i did some user error or hit a bug with the llvm tooling (not sure if the coverage tooling can deal with symbols that have more than one definition)."
                }
            ],
